{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "0f12b1a9-7c69-51d1-ab4a-ad4778d97aeb"/*PhysicsVolumeGravityExample*/,
  "Description": "A volume can be a force as well as a collider. [VolumeToField] turns the torus volume into a vector field, its gradient, and a [RigidForce] of type Field samples that field at every body. Negative Strength pulls the boxes towards the surface instead of pushing them away. The same volume, meshed with [VolumeToMesh], is the collider they land on. World gravity is zero.\n\nAKA: gravity well, attractor, magnet, field force, volume gradient\n\nTips\n- Playback must run for the simulation to advance; press Reset on the World to start over.\n- Any [VectorField] works as a force: noise, curl, or a field built from SDF operators.",
